  "limitations": [
    "One top-level pair of manual approval then unbound literal native checkout branches with failFast true and identity-derived directories.",
    "Cancellation is observed while the sibling remains at an undecided input; interruption of an already-running checkout and cancellation latency are not certified.",
    "The observer controls approval order and reads native directory ownership, fixed marker paths, join and original error origin; it does not prove simultaneous CPU or Git activity.",
    "The first root clone removes preceding branch directories; no workspace survival, export, artifact transfer, state continuity, security, freshness or cross-build guarantee.",
    "No nested or arbitrary branch work, human authorization, generic support promotion or portable execution. The disposable runtime host and observer remain trusted."
  ]
